From 9024a4b1ee5e73515203d5560ed76132b1615447 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:24:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Sync merge safety: per-path first-snapshot defence,
 attached echoes, per-leaf drafts, per-field meta
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes verified by the 2026-10-26 reliability audit (RESULTS-G1/G2):
- sync#1 (critical): the first snapshot's 'defend offline work' branch pushed
  the WHOLE local tree over newer server data; it now diffs against the tree
  as loaded and sends only this device's own paths.
- sync#3/scoring#1: an identical idle re-fetch replaced every synced object,
  detaching open tally/bracket/notice views so later taps were silently lost;
  identical echoes now keep the live objects.
- sync#4: tally drafts diffed per score leaf (two scorers no longer wipe
  each other); sync#6: meta per field, hiddenCards per card.
- sync#7: adopting the first snapshot clears dataEditPending.
- sync#8: healing RTDB pruning no longer re-pushes the whole config.
- scoring#4: verse/cleanup points use deterministic ids (no 3+5=8).
- sync#2: only real Jelly form controls count as typing — a focused card
  header no longer freezes live updates on Android/desktop Chrome.
- sync#5/time#3/time#6: the deploy auto-reload waits for unconfirmed
  writes, a running Pictionary lap, and a chat message in progress.
- auth#3: camp switch / sign-out ask before discarding an unconfirmed score.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
