From 689faa546af5c2072df14dfc1219447774ec052e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:29:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Chat reliability: serialized sends, no rebuild on window
 slide, back-fill not re-announced

Fixes verified by the 2026-10-26 audit (RESULTS-G3), reproduced with the real
SDK + emulator and in Chromium:
- chat#1: sends go out one at a time, each a full CHAT_MIN_SEND_MS after the
  previous ACK, so a caption typed during a photo upload (or an offline burst)
  is no longer refused by the 1 s rules floor; the words are given back to
  the CURRENT composer if a send still fails.
- chat#2: in a full channel the sliding window removes one bubble instead of
  rebuilding the view (which wiped the draft and dropped the keyboard);
  same-channel rebuilds carry draft, cursor, focus and scroll across.
- chat#3: messages arriving while the tab is hidden are drawn (not marked read).
- chat#4: a back-filled old message is not re-announced or appended last.
- chat#5: the 30 s tick no longer rebuilds an unchanged announcement composer.
- chat#6: channel badges refresh on every message; marking seen covers the
  newest message on screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FmwrSqURuVRaeeP3mUmmwi
