Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Alerts hardening (app side): retrying chat notify, honest
 sender status, push-host allowlist in the rules
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From the app-side review:
- pushNotifyChat retries network/timeout/429/5xx twice (2 s, 6 s; the Worker
  dedupes by msgId) with keepalive, and an Announcements poster is told if
  phone alerts may not have gone out — nothing else re-sends a chat alert.
- The director's sender line no longer shows green when the sender's
  signing key is broken (/health vapid:false / ok:false).
- database.rules.json: a push endpoint must be a real push service
  (google.com/googleapis.com, Apple, Mozilla, Windows) — verified in the
  RTDB emulator (5 real hosts accepted; look-alikes and plain http refused).
- Two vacuous tests made real: sw.js's https-only sender URL check now runs
  with a real URL API; the dormant drawer test checks what was drawn.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FmwrSqURuVRaeeP3mUmmwi
